    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Host Memory and Swap Tiers",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "grafana-postgresql-datasource",
        "uid": "tomoribot-postgres"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 7
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "unit": "decmbytes"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "grafana-postgresql-datasource",
            "uid": "tomoribot-postgres"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "format": "time_series",
          "rawQuery": true,
          "rawSql": "SELECT created_at AS \"time\",\n       (fields->>'swapfile_used_mb')::float AS swapfile_used_mb,\n       (fields->>'zram_used_mb')::float     AS zram_used_mb,\n       (fields->>'host_avail_mb')::float    AS host_avail_mb\nFROM metric_samples\nWHERE metric_name = 'host_memory' AND $__timeFilter(created_at)\nORDER BY created_at",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Host memory split by swap tier. zram and the disk-backed /swapfile differ by roughly 100x in fault cost, so the aggregate cannot say whether the host is merely compressing or actually paging to disk. A rising swapfile_used_mb is the expensive case. swapon reports uncompressed size and cannot make this distinction."
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Host Pressure (PSI) and Swap-In Rate",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "grafana-postgresql-datasource",
        "uid": "tomoribot-postgres"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 7
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 4,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "grafana-postgresql-datasource",
            "uid": "tomoribot-postgres"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "format": "time_series",
          "rawQuery": true,
          "rawSql": "SELECT created_at AS \"time\",\n       (fields->>'io_full_avg60')::float  AS io_full_avg60,\n       (fields->>'mem_full_avg60')::float AS mem_full_avg60,\n       (fields->>'swap_in_per_s')::float  AS swap_in_per_s\nFROM metric_samples\nWHERE metric_name = 'host_memory' AND $__timeFilter(created_at)\nORDER BY created_at",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "description": "PSI full is the share of wall time every task was blocked, and io_full is the signal that tracked every host incident in this deployment. swap_in_per_s separates a large swap level that is merely cold pages evicted once (harmless) from a working set that is genuinely oversubscribed. The first sample after a restart carries no rate."
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Pool Retirements by Code",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "grafana-postgresql-datasource",
        "uid": "tomoribot-postgres"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 14,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 7
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 4,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "grafana-postgresql-datasource",
            "uid": "tomoribot-postgres"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "format": "time_series",
          "rawQuery": true,
          "rawSql": "SELECT created_at AS \"time\",\n       (fields->>'pool_lifetime_5m')::int AS lifetime_timeout,\n       (fields->>'pool_idle_5m')::int     AS idle_timeout,\n       (fields->>'pool_other_5m')::int    AS other\nFROM metric_samples\nWHERE metric_name = 'host_memory' AND $__timeFilter(created_at)\nORDER BY created_at",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Connections Bun retired out from under a live query (oven-sh/bun#30646), counted per 5 minute sample. Read this against the host panels above: a cascade that tracks swap and PSI is a different problem from one that fires at a healthy memory reading. Retirements at some rate are normal and are not by themselves a fault; see the retry panel."
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Pool Retry Outcome",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "grafana-postgresql-datasource",
        "uid": "tomoribot-postgres"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 8,
        "y": 14,
