      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "grafana-postgresql-datasource",
            "uid": "tomoribot-postgres"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "format": "time_series",
          "rawQuery": true,
          "rawSql": "SELECT created_at AS \"time\",\n       (fields->>'pool_retries_recovered_5m')::int AS recovered,\n       (fields->>'pool_retries_exhausted_5m')::int AS exhausted\nFROM metric_samples\nWHERE metric_name = 'host_memory' AND $__timeFilter(created_at)\nORDER BY created_at",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "description": "The panel that says whether users felt anything. Recovered retirements were absorbed by withTransientDbRetry and cost only latency; only exhausted ones reach a user as a failed turn or a Database Unreachable notice. Rising exhausted against flat recovered is a retry budget decision (POSTGRES_TRANSIENT_RETRY_ATTEMPTS), not a pool timeout one."
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Lifetime Retirement Phase",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "grafana-postgresql-datasource",
        "uid": "tomoribot-postgres"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 16,
        "y": 14,
